  "body": "Part of #1490. Found while working #2031 (the motion-crate generator `camcraft_motion::machining2d::rest_adaptive`).\n\nWhat happens: the rest Adaptive plan is correct and holds the load, but it travels a lot out of cut. Measured (debug build, 4 mm tool after a 12 mm tool, two depths; cut / air feed / rapid in mm):\n\n| Fixture | Passes a depth | Plunges a depth | Cut | Air feed | Rapid |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 60 x 40 pocket, 3 mm corners | 40 | 4 | 224 | 967 | 360 |\n| 70 x 50 with a 14 x 14 island | 36 | 4 | 250 | 955 | 450 |\n| two 30 x 30 bays, 10 mm neck | 128 | 37 | 954 | 3445 | 1337 |\n\nWhy: the verifier's crossing law reads exact signs, so a pass that rides a wall retraces the area's first way in and first way out on the wall's own vertices, and returns on one chord (`adaptive/rest/leads.rs`, `canon.rs`). Every pass of a corner pays that wall ride and the return. In a neck, a half loop whose return would cross an earlier feed is reached by a retract instead. The plain Adaptive holds its plans to 1.5 times the cut length out of cut and 8 retract hops a level (`pocket_hsm::over_budget`); rest Adaptive is not held to that yet. The posted path is chords only (no arc fit): 3216 moves for the corner fixture, 14850 for the neck.\n\nIdeas, none tried: shorten the retrace to the previous pass's landing instead of the area's first; lifted returns as the plain Adaptive's (`adaptive/lift.rs`); arcs fitted and proved inside the center area (`arc_proof.rs`) with the load re-read on the fitted path.\n\nDone means: rest Adaptive is held to a stated out-of-cut and retract budget (the plain Adaptive's, or a recorded one of its own) with a named refusal or fallback past it; the readings above are re-measured and recorded; every law of `crates/motion/tests/rest_adaptive/` still holds.\n",
